<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n10542" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">con-sŏcĭus</span></b> , a,
		um, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>adj.,
				united, connected</i> (late Lat.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">elementa sibi valde,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Fulg. Myth. 1, 2</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Subst.
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">consŏ-cĭus</span></b> , ii,
			m., <i>a partaker, aid, companion</i> (with
			consortes), <i><span class="en">Cod. Just. 10, 2, 3</span></i>; Firm.
			Math. 3, 13, 1.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">consŏcĭa</span></b> ,
				ae, f., <i>a female
				companion, consort</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">consors totius vitae et consocia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ambros. Ep. 9, 70</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
